anytime.</p>\\n    </form>\\n  </section>\\n\\n  <section class=\\\"about\\\">\\n    <h2>About YogaDirect</h2>\\n    <p>Thanks to our loyal customers, YogaDirect has become one of the largest suppliers of yoga mats and props in the country. We have been faithfully supplying the Yoga community since 1999 and are confident that we can help you grow your studio, event, or personal practice with everything you need and more. We manufacture and source our own goods which is how we can consistently offer high-quality yoga gear at amazing prices. When you shop at YogaDirect, feel proud in knowing that you are helping to grow not only your business or personal practice but the Yoga community as a whole. From our team of Yoga lovers to you, thank you.</p>\\n  </section>\\n</div>\\n\\n<footer class=\\\"site\\\">\\n  <div class=\\\"container\\\">\\n    <div class=\\\"cols\\\">\\n      <div>\\n        <h4>Shop</h4>\\n        <ul>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"/yoga-mats\\\">Yoga Mats</a></li>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"/yoga-blocks\\\">Yoga Blocks</a></li>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"/yoga-straps\\\">Yoga Straps</a></li>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"/kits\\\">Kits &amp; Sets</a></li>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"/sale\\\">Sale</a></li>\\n        </ul>\\n      </div>\\n      <div>\\n        <h4>Customer Service</h4>\\n        <ul>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"/contact\\\">Contact Us</a></li>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"/shipping\\\">Shipping Info</a></li>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"/returns\\\">Returns</a></li>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"/faq\\\">FAQ</a></li>\\n        </ul>\\n      </div>\\n      <div>\\n        <h4>Company</h4>\\n        <ul>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"/about\\\">About Us</a></li>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"/wholesale\\\">Wholesale &amp; Studios</a></li>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"/privacy\\\">Privacy Policy</a></li>\\n          <li><a href=\\\"/terms\\\">Terms of Use</a></li>\\n        </ul>\\n      </div>\\n      <div class=\\\"HDLmClassEA09E48A\\\">\\n        <h4>10% off + yoga deals by email</h4>\\n        <p style=\\\"margin:0 0 10px\\\">Subscribe and we&rsquo;ll email your 10% off code right away.</p>\\n        <form class=\\\"foot-form\\\" action=\\\"/email-signup\\\" method=\\\"post\\\">\\n          <label for=\\\"footEmail\\\" style=\\\"position:absolute;left:-9999px\\\">Email address</label>\\n          <input id=\\\"footEmail\\\" type=\\\"email\\\" name=\\\"email\\\" required placeholder=\\\"Enter your email\\\">\\n          <button class=\\\"btn\\\" type=\\\"submit\\\">Get 10% Off</button>\\n        </form>\\n      </div>\\n    </div>\\n    <div class=\\\"legal\\\">&copy; 1999&ndash;2024 YogaDirect.com. All rights reserved.</div>\\n  </div>\\n</footer>\\n\\n<div class=\\\"modal-backdrop HDLmClassEA09E48A\\\" id=\\\"emailOfferModal\\\" role=\\\"dialog\\\" aria-modal=\\\"true\\\" aria-labelledby=\\\"emailModalTitle\\\">\\n  <div class=\\\"modal\\\">\\n    <button class=\\\"modal-close\\\" type=\\\"button\\\" aria-label=\\\"Close\\\" onclick=\\\"closeEmailOffer()\\\">&times;</button>\\n    <h2 id=\\\"emailModalTitle\\\">Save 10% on your first order</h2>\\n    <p>Enter your email and we&rsquo;ll send your discount code plus first access to new arrivals and sales.</p>\\n    <form class=\\\"email-form\\\" action=\\\"/email-signup\\\" method=\\\"post\\\">\\n      <label for=\\\"modalEmail\\\" style=\\\"position:absolute;left:-9999px\\\">Email address</label>\\n      <input id=\\\"modalEmail\\\" type=\\\"email\\\" name=\\\"email\\\" required placeholder=\\\"you@example.com\\\">\\n      <button class=\\\"btn\\\" type=\\\"submit\\\">Email My 10% Code</button>\\n      <p class=\\\"fineprint\\\">New customers only. Unsubscribe anytime.</p>\\n    </form>\\n    <button class=\\\"no-thanks\\\" type=\\\"button\\\" onclick=\\\"closeEmailOffer()\\\">No thanks, I&rsquo;ll pay full price</button>\\n  </div>\\n</div>\\n\\n<script>\\n(function(){\\n  function shown(){try{return localStorage.getItem('yd_email_offer')==='1'}catch(e){return false}}\\n  function mark(){try{localStorage.setItem('yd_email_offer','1')}catch(e){}}\\n  window.closeEmailOffer=function(){var m=document.getElementById('emailOfferModal');if(m){m.classList.remove('open')}mark()};\\n  if(!shown()){\\n    var opened=false;\\n    function open(){if(opened||shown())return;opened=true;document.getElementById('emailOfferModal').classList.add('open')}\\n    setTimeout(open,12000);\\n    document.addEventListener('mouseout',function(e){if(!e.relatedTarget&&e.clientY<10){open()}});\\n  }\\n})();\\n</script>\\n\\n</body>\\n</html>\",\"improvements\":[{\"What\":\"Added an email offer with 10% off the first order\",\"Why\":\"Captures visitor emails to enable follow-up marketing and the discount incentive increases first-order conversions\",\"Hash\":\"HDLmClassEA09E48A\"}]}","refusal":null,"reasoning":"The fetch only returned plain text instead of HTML, so I need to reconstruct the page structure from scratch. Since I'm only adding an email offer as requested, I'll build HTML with an email signup banner or popup that includes a discount incentive. Now I'm calculating the DJB2 hash for verification. Computing the DJB2 hash step by step, working through each character of the concatenated string and applying the modulo operation to keep the values manageable. Continuing through the hash computation with each character, tracking the modular arithmetic at each step to keep the values within the 32-bit range. Continuing the hash calculations... Continuing through the hash computation for the remaining characters, processing '1', '0', '%', and ' ' with their respective ASCII values and modular arithmetic operations. Continuing through the hash calculations for the remaining characters in the string, working through the modular arithmetic for 't', 'h', and 'e'. Continuing through the hash calculations for the remaining characters in \"first ot\", tracking the modular arithmetic and differences at each step. Continuing with the hash calculations for \"Capture\" — working through each character's contribution to the running hash value, applying the multiplication and modulo operations at each step. Continuing through the hash computation for 's', space, 'v', and 'i' characters, tracking the modular arithmetic and intermediate values as the algorithm processes each character in the string. Continuing through the hash computation for the remaining characters: 'o', 'r', space, and 'e', applying the same modular arithmetic pattern with multiplications by 33 and successive modulo operations against powers of 2. Continuing through the character sequence, processing 's', space, 't', and 'o' with the same modular arithmetic operations, tracking the running hash value as each character gets multiplied, shifted, and reduced. Continuing through the hash computation for the remaining characters in \"enable\", tracking the modular arithmetic operations and intermediate values as each character gets processed. Continuing the hash computation... Continuing the hash calculation... Continuing through the character calculations with modular arithmetic, working through 'n', 'd', ' ', and 't' to track the running hash values and their differences from powers of 2. Continuing through the character sequence, processing 'i', 's', 'c', 'o' with their ASCII values and applying the same modular arithmetic operations to track the running hash value. Continuing the hash calculations... Continuing through the character encoding calculations for 'i', 'n', 'c', and 'r'. Continuing through the hash computation for the remaining characters in \"ease \". Continuing through the character calculations for 'o', 'r', 'd', and 'e', tracking the modular arithmetic operations and subtracting powers of 2 at each step to keep the values manageable. Continuing through the character sequence, processing 'v', 'e', 'r', 's' with the same rolling hash calculations, multiplying by 33 and adjusting with modulo operations to track the hash state. Now I'm converting the final hash value to hexadecimal by repeatedly dividing by powers of 16 and extracting each digit.\n\nI've got the complete hex representation: EA09E48A. So the full hash class becomes HDLmClassEA09E48A.\n\nNow I need to build out the HTML for the YogaDirect homepage. Since I only have the text content and not the original HTML file, I'll reconstruct a complete page with header, navigation, hero section, featured products, the about section, and footer — making sure to integrate the email offer banner, modal, and signup form all marked with that hash class identifier.","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","signature":"","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0},{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The fetch only returned plain text instead of HTML, so I need to reconstruct the page structure from scratch. Since I'm only adding an email offer as requested, I'll build HTML with an email signup banner or popup that includes a discount incentive. Now I'm calculating the DJB2 hash for verification. Computing the DJB2 hash step by step, working through each character of the concatenated string and applying the modulo operation to keep the values manageable. Continuing through the hash computation with each character, tracking the modular arithmetic at each step to keep the values within the 32-bit range. Continuing the hash calculations... Continuing through the hash computation for the remaining characters, processing '1', '0', '%', and ' ' with their respective ASCII values and modular arithmetic operations. Continuing through the hash calculations for the remaining characters in the string, working through the modular arithmetic for 't', 'h', and 'e'. Continuing through the hash calculations for the remaining characters in \"first ot\", tracking the modular arithmetic and differences at each step. Continuing with the hash calculations for \"Capture\" — working through each character's contribution to the running hash value, applying the multiplication and modulo operations at each step. Continuing through the hash computation for 's', space, 'v', and 'i' characters, tracking the modular arithmetic and intermediate values as the algorithm processes each character in the string. Continuing through the hash computation for the remaining characters: 'o', 'r', space, and 'e', applying the same modular arithmetic pattern with multiplications by 33 and successive modulo operations against powers of 2. Continuing through the character sequence, processing 's', space, 't', and 'o' with the same modular arithmetic operations, tracking the running hash value as each character gets multiplied, shifted, and reduced. Continuing through the hash computation for the remaining characters in \"enable\", tracking the modular arithmetic operations and intermediate values as each character gets processed. Continuing the hash computation... Continuing the hash calculation... Continuing through the character calculations with modular arithmetic, working through 'n', 'd', ' ', and 't' to track the running hash values and their differences from powers of 2. Continuing through the character sequence, processing 'i', 's', 'c', 'o' with their ASCII values and applying the same modular arithmetic operations to track the running hash value. Continuing the hash calculations... Continuing through the character encoding calculations for 'i', 'n', 'c', and 'r'. Continuing through the hash computation for the remaining characters in \"ease \". Continuing through the character calculations for 'o', 'r', 'd', and 'e', tracking the modular arithmetic operations and subtracting powers of 2 at each step to keep the values manageable. Continuing through the character sequence, processing 'v', 'e', 'r', 's' with the same rolling hash calculations, multiplying by 33 and adjusting with modulo operations to track the hash state. Now I'm converting the final hash value to hexadecimal by repeatedly dividing by powers of 16 and extracting each digit.\n\nI've got the complete hex representation: EA09E48A. So the full hash class becomes HDLmClassEA09E48A.\n\nNow I need to build out the HTML for the YogaDirect homepage. Since I only have the text content and not the original HTML file, I'll reconstruct a complete page with header, navigation, hero section, featured products, the about section, and footer — making sure to integrate the email offer banner, modal, and signup form all marked with that hash class identifier.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":1,"signature":""}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":3947,"completion_tokens":18848,"total_tokens":22795,"cost":0.490935,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.490935,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.019735,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.4712},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":935,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0},"server_tool_use_details":{"web_search_requests":0}}}
